=== Prompt ===
Who is Che Guevara?

=== Response ===
Che Guevara (June 14, 1928 – October 9, 1967) was an Argentine Marxist revolutionary, physician, author, guerrilla leader, diplomat, and military theorist. A key figure in the Cuban Revolution, he worked with Fidel Castro and helped to overthrow the US-backed Batista regime.

Guevara played a central role in the early years of the Cuban Revolution, serving in various positions in the Cuban government, including Minister of Industries, and as an adviser to Castro. He was instrumental in the agrarian reform in Cuba, which redistributed land from large landowners to landless farmers.

After the Cuban Revolution, Guevara traveled to various parts of the world to promote revolutionary movements, particularly in Africa and Latin America. He was a vocal critic of imperialism and capitalism and advocated for the establishment of socialist governments in developing countries.

In 1967, Guevara was captured and executed by the Bolivian military while attempting to foment a revolution in that country. He has become a symbol of the revolutionary left and a cultural icon, with his image appearing on posters, T-shirts, and other merchandise around the world.

